==Battleground==
*The enemy base here is an [[Aku Altar (Enemy Base)|Aku Altar]].
*5 [[Aku Doge]]s spawn after 13.33 seconds<sup>400f</sup>, delay 10~13.33 seconds<sup>300f~400f</sup>.
*3 [[Sinner Snache]]s spawn after 13.33 seconds<sup>400f</sup>, delay 16.67~20 seconds<sup>500f~600f</sup>.
*10 [[Cerberus Kids]] spawn after 13.33 seconds<sup>400f</sup>, delay 3.33~6.67 seconds<sup>100f~200f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Wicked Face]] spawns as the boss.
**Infinite [[Cerberus Kids]] spawn, delay 10~20 seconds<sup>300f~600f</sup>.
**5 [[Aku Doge]]s spawn, delay 30~40 seconds<sup>900f~1,200f</sup>.
**1 [[Fallen Bear]] spawns.
**3 [[Cerberus Kids]] spawn, delay 0.07 seconds<sup>2f</sup>.
**3 [[Sinner Snache]]s spawn, delay 0.07 seconds<sup>2f</sup>.
**3 [[Aku Doge]]s spawn, delay 0.07 seconds<sup>2f</sup>.
**5 [[Aku Gory|Aku Gories]] spawn, delay 20~23.33 seconds<sup>600f~700f</sup>.
**5 [[Condemned Peng]]s spawn, delay 13.33~16.67 seconds<sup>400f~500f</sup>.

==Strategy==
With its relentless spam of high DPS Aku enemies and a Wicked Face with an absurd 200% strength magnification, this stage is quite vicious. As such, it's not recommended to challenge it until most of the other Aku Realms stages are beaten; Level 40 is the recommended minimum before making any attempts. It is best to bring any and all anti-Aku cats you have as well as any [[:category:Cats with Freeze Immunity|Freeze]] and/or [[:category:Cats with Wave Immunity|Wave Immune]] attackers for the Wicked Face. [[:category:Cats with Surge Immunity|Surge Immune]] cats are also extremely valuable due to the large number of [[Death Surge|Death Surges]] present in the stage, especially if they're [[:Category:Meatshield-class Cats|meatshields]] like Talented [[Boogie Cat (Special Cat)|Gato Amigo]].

==='''Recommended Units'''===
*Talented [[Boogie Cat (Special Cat)|Gato Amigo]]: With his Immune to Surge talent unlocked, Gato Amigo becomes a near-mandatory pick for this stage thanks to his cheap cost and accessibility.
*[[Ancient Egg: N003 (Special Cat)|Cat Cactus]]: Another amazing pick for a meatshield thanks to its resistance to Aku and Surge Immunity.
*Talented [[Matador Cat (Rare Cat)|Bellydancer Cat]]: If her Target Aku talent is unlocked, Bellydancer shines in this stage due to it being comprised purely of Aku enemies. However, be mindful of her high cost, as she can drain cash if you're not careful.
*[[Aku Researcher (Rare Cat)|Evil Aku Researcher]]: Arguably the most accessible Shield Piercer, who also benefits from being fast and cheap.
*[[Slime Cat (Rare Cat)|Jelly Dumpling Cat]]: A cheap attacker who is able to help get rid of the peons at the beginning and chip down the backline attackers. Its True Form is recommended more thanks to its better range and ability to one-shot Aku Doge.
*[[Stone Cat (Rare Cat)|Stone Cat]]: Stone's nature as a suicidal meatshield gives him the ability to hold the line well, especially against Aku Gory's Savage Blows.
*[[Maize Cat (Rare Cat)|Maize Cat]]: If somehow owned at the time the player challenges this stage, Maize can perform amazingly thanks to his high health against Aku and immunity to Freeze, letting him take on Wicked Face. Do take note of his lack of Surge Immunity, however.
*[[Ancient Egg: N109 (Rare Cat)|Barrel Cat]]: Serves as one of the best options for a non-Uber Shield Piercer thanks to his Surge Immunity combined with his Long Distance, letting him snipe the shields of Fallen Bear and Wicked Face.
*[[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cat]]: A spammable high DPS unit. Can Can is even more recommended if his Move Speed Up and especially Double Bounty talents are unlocked.
*[[Weightlifter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Pizza Cat]]: Pizza Cat's high durability and solid power makes him a good option for this stage, even with the lack of Dark enemies.
*[[Brainwashed Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Brainwashed Cat]]: Essentially a better version of Talented Bellydancer Cat, he has the same 30% chance to [[Dodge]] Aku for 2 seconds, but is much cheaper and faster.
*[[Crazed Gross Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic Macho Legs]]: If one lacks Jelly Dumpling Cat, Manic Macho Legs serves as a good alternative Waver, especially given his superior range and bulk.
*[[Nymph Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Fiend Cat]]: His chance to knockback Aku and piercing LD mean he can seriously help with preserving ground. His DPS is nothing to scoff at, either. However, he suffers from low HP and mediocre range. His Resistance talent offsets his health problem, but his range means he should not be sent out carelessly.

==='''Recommended Ubers'''===
Generally, any Uber with [[:category:Anti-Aku Cats|anti-Aku]] and/or [[:Category:Shield Piercing Cats|Shield Piercing]] abilities will do at least a decent job in this stage. However, the best picks among them are:
* [[Agent Staal (Uber Rare Cat)|Edgemaster Staal]]: Staal's high damage against Aku, fast attack rate, and Immunity to Freeze and Surge as well as his chance to Pierce Shields allows him to utterly shred through this stage.
*[[Empress Chronos (Uber Rare Cat)|Empress Chronos]]: Can ease the enemies' pushing power thanks to her Freeze ability, and is immune to Wicked Face's own Freeze. However, she's highly vulnerable to the Death Surges present throughout the stage.
*[[Hevijak the Wicked (Uber Rare Cat)|Hevijak the Wicked]]: Serves as a durable anti-Aku crowd conntroller and shield piercer, being especially good at dealing with the Aku Gories. He becomes even better at his job when True Formed and with his Wave Immune talent unlocked, letting him handle Wicked Face with ease.
*[[Yamii (Uber Rare Cat)|Yaminora]]: A phenomenal support unit for this stage thanks to his high health against Aku and Wave Blocker ability. Do note that he is unable to outrange Wicked Face, however.
*[[Keiji Claus (Uber Rare Cat)|Maeda Christmas DX]]: While his True Form is expensive, he functions as an excellent tank not unlike Hevijak, all while having Wave Immune right out of the box. He becomes even better with his Strengthen and especially Immune to Surge talents unlocked; however, do be sure to support him with plenty of Shield Piercers.
*[[Kaoru Hanayama (Uber Rare Cat)|Kaoru Hanayama]]: Hanayama's high health, immunity to Freeze and Slow, and absurd damage against Aku makes him a natural pick for this stage.

